00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,170
I called them,

269
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:44,390
the last train leaves in a half-hour.

270
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,340
And I have a massage client soon.

271
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:49,190
You guys, just, please, a little bit longer.

272
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,100
I promise,

273
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,830
Rachel will be back with the cake any minute.

274
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:55,050
Monica, remember the frosting, huh?

275
00:12:55,710 --> 00:12:57,340
All right, five more minutes.

276
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,450
Hello?

277
00:13:02,390 --> 00:13:03,830
Oh, no, what happened?

278
00:13:04,510 --> 00:13:06,770
Okay, okay, where are you?

279
00:13:07,230 --> 00:13:08,920
Okay, I'll be right there.

280
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:10,540
Was that Emma?

281
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,180
Is she up?

282
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,580
Rachel got pulled over for speeding.

283
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:16,080
She forgot her license.

284
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:16,990
I have to bring it to her.

285
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,410
If you're leaving, I'm definitely going.

286
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:22,460
Wait, if anybody gets to go, it's us!

287
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,410
We've been complaining the longest!

288
00:13:25,350 --> 00:13:27,930
No, wait, you guys. No, you can't leave.

289
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,880
Rachel already feels bad that the cake's messed up.

290
00:13:30,930 --> 00:13:33,050
How do you think she'll feel

291
00:13:33,050 --> 00:13:34,030
when she comes back and you're gone?

292
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,510
I don't know. You'll tell us on Monday.

293
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:40,770
Joey, you're in charge, okay?

294
00:13:40,770 --> 00:13:41,940
You make sure nobody leaves.

295
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:43,260
Got it!

296
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:47,350
Hey! Where do you think you're going?

297
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,910
To the bathroom.

298
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:51,060
Well, the rest of you get comfortable,

299
00:13:51,110 --> 00:13:52,970
because we are gonna be here for a--

300
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:55,260
Wait, there's a window in there.

301
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:57,940
No! He's not getting away that easy!

302
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:01,440
What are you doing?

303
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,430
Get the hell out of here!

304
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:11,750
Well, that one did not have Emma's face on it.

305
00:14:12,630 --> 00:14:14,330
- No, it did not. - No.

306
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:17,890
Well, we'd better get going. It's late.

307
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,750
Jack can't drive at night anymore.

308
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:21,550
He has trouble staying in his lane.

309
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,650
Last winter I went up on a church lawn

310
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,690
and drove right through a manger scene.

311
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:27,840
The papers thought it was a hate crime.

312
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,620
- Anyway, it was lovely seeing you. - Okay.

313
00:14:34,670 --> 00:14:37,080
- Bye. Bye, dear. - Nighty-night.

314
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:38,750
- Nighty-night. - Bye.

315
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:41,420
How could you just let them leave?

316
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:42,100
Hey, hey, hey.

317
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:43,460
I'm not gonna mess with Jack.

318
00:14:43,510 --> 00:14:45,460
He's a great man. He fought for our country.

319
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:47,420
No, he didn't.

320
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,710
He pretended to be a Quaker

321
00:14:48,710 --> 00:14:49,840
to get out of Korea.

322
00:14:51,490 --> 00:14:54,200
Well, that's it. He's the last one to go.

323
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,290
I'm locking you guys in.

324
00:14:56,340 --> 00:14:57,710
You do know I can just turn them

325
00:14:57,710 --> 00:14:59,080
the other way around, right?

326
00:15:00,230 --> 00:15:02,370
Oh, I forgot you used to live here.

327
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:10,690
- Hello? - Joey, it's Estelle.

328
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:14,070
- Hey. - So how'd your audition go today?

329
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,490
What audition?

330
00:15:15,490 --> 00:15:17,630
The one I told you about last week.

331
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,900
What? You never said anything about an audition.

332
00:15:23,510 --> 00:15:25,510
Let me start over.

333
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:28,030
I just got a call about an audition.

334
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:30,780
I think you can still make it.

335
00:15:30,830 --> 00:15:32,950
It's down at the Astor Theater,

336
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,100
and you need to have a monologue prepared.

337
00:15:35,150 --> 00:15:37,290
A monologue? I don't have a--

338
00:15:41,070 --> 00:15:42,280
I got it.

339
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:46,630
So I'm gonna take off.

340
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,420
What?

341
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:49,180
No, wait! You don't get to leave.

342
00:15:49,230 --> 00:15:52,450
I've got a massage client waiting outside my door any minute.

343
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,490
And we paid for a room

344
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:55,650
that we're supposed to be in right now!

345
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:57,190
Well, okay, now...

346
00:15:57,590 --> 00:15:59,840
...only one of us has to stay with Emma.

347
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:03,390
Okay, and as the person who realized that, I get to go.

348
00:16:03,910 --> 00:16:05,680
No...

349
00:16:05,890 --> 00:16:08,560
Let's figure out a fair way to decide who's staying.

350
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:10,720
Oh, I got it.

351
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,750
Okay, everyone pick a number from one to 10, all right?

352
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:16,690
Whoever gets the highest number gets to go first.

353
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,610
Okay, 10.

354
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:21,570
Okay, Monica picks 10. I call nine.

355
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:22,800
Anyone else?

356
00:16:24,310 --> 00:16:27,160
- No, let's just draw straws. - Okay.

357
00:16:27,210 --> 00:16:29,250
Or we could flip a coin and multiply the answer--

358
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,670
- I'm begging you to stop. - Right.

359
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:33,670
Okay, how about this?

360
00:16:33,770 --> 00:16:35,870
We got wind-up toys for Emma.

361
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,020
We can make them race,

362
00:16:37,020 --> 00:16:39,410
and whoever comes in last stays.

363
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,160
Yeah, let's do that!

364
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,150
That sounds more fun than the thing

365
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:44,750
we were gonna do in Vermont!

366
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:47,560
Okay, everybody, pick your toys!

367
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,890
Okay. I want the dolphin!

368
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:51,110
- That's a bear! - I'm too excited!

369
00:16:52,670 --> 00:16:54,320
Phoebe, you get the bear.

370
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,660
Joey, you get the robot.

371
00:16:55,710 --> 00:16:56,680
Oh, yeah.

372
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:57,890
And Chandler and I get the dog.

373
00:16:57,940 --> 00:17:02,450
And the race is going to go from here to here.

374
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:05,860
Now, the one who comes in last stays!

375
00:17:05,910 --> 00:17:07,240
Okay, ladies and gentlemen,

376
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,120
wind your toys.

377
00:17:08,310 --> 00:17:11,640
Okay. On your mark, get set, go!

378
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,750
Go! Go!

379
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,450
Come on, robot!

380
00:17:16,330 --> 00:17:18,320
What are you barking at?

381
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:26,590
Well, how is that gonna help?

382
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,370
I bought you!

383
00:17:28,370 --> 00:17:30,730
How did I forget that that's all you do?

384
00:17:31,290 --> 00:17:33,540
Way to go, robot!

385
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:35,630
Good job, Alan.

386
00:17:36,850 --> 00:17:38,020
Hey, good race, you guys.

387
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:39,190
Yeah, see you later.

388
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:41,410
No. No, no. Wait.

389
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,190
We didn't lose.

390
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:44,870
The rules clearly stated that

391
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,880
the last one to cross the finish line was the loser.

392
00:17:47,930 --> 00:17:49,080
Well, our dog never crossed

393
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:51,230
the finish line. So technically--

394
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,420
They left.

395
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,170
There isn't time to go to the bakery.

396
00:18:00,170 --> 00:18:01,810
We're gonna come home.

397
00:18:02,350 --> 00:18:04,060
Everybody left?

398
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:06,670
All right. Well, just tell Emma

399
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:09,560
that we'll be there as soon as we can. Bye.

400
00:18:11,370 --> 00:18:13,500
- Rachel! - Oh, God, sorry!

401
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:15,030
I can't believe they gave you a ticket.

402
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:16,500
You're such a good driver.

403
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:21,570
- Emma's awake. - Yeah?

404
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,090
I can't believe this.

405
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,050
This is her first birthday,

406
00:18:26,050 --> 00:18:27,740
she's awake, we're not even there.

407
00:18:27,790 --> 00:18:29,460
Everybody left.

408
00:18:29,470 --> 00:18:31,140
We still have this stupid obscene cake.

409
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:32,920
Hey, maybe I can fix that.

410
00:18:32,970 --> 00:18:35,080
You know, try to turn it into something else.

411
00:18:35,130 --> 00:18:37,540
Oh, don't even bother.

412
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:40,060
We've already ruined her first birthday.

413
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,040
And do you know

414
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:43,000
how important these early experiences are,

415
00:18:43,050 --> 00:18:44,500
Ross? Very!

416
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:47,390
According to the back cover of that book that you gave me.

417
00:18:49,030 --> 00:18:51,200
Rach, she's not gonna remember this.

418
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:54,400
I guess.

419
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:57,510
Oh, I just had such an idea

420
00:18:57,520 --> 00:19:00,590
of what this day would be like, you know?

421
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:03,030
Emma laughing...

422
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,680
...and everybody gathered around her cake,

423
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,680
singing "Happy Birthday."

424
00:19:08,010 --> 00:19:09,080
And then we would all--

425
00:19:09,130 --> 00:19:11,380
Hey, get out of the road,

426
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:12,130
you stupid student driver!

427
00:19:14,130 --> 00:19:15,670
They have to learn.

428
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,820
- Hey. - What?

429
00:19:19,870 --> 00:19:21,210
This is not bad.

430
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:23,650
Oh, my God. Look, you made it into a bunny.

431
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:27,060
How did you do that?

432
00:19:27,110 --> 00:19:30,450
Well, I just made these two things cheeks.

433
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:35,400
And then I split this to make ears.

434
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,570
Well, I am very impressed.

435
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:40,880
Some can sing, some can dance.

436
00:19:40,930 --> 00:19:42,020
I, apparently, can turn phallic cakes

437
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:44,200
into woodland creatures.

438
00:19:46,630 --> 00:19:49,800
Now, another way to organize your stuffed animals

439
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,070
is by size.

440
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,340
I'm sorry, is this a game

441
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,120
for Emma or for Monica?

442
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:56,740
Game?

443
00:19:57,420 --> 00:20:00,690
Emma, do you even know it's your birthday today?

444
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:01,780
You're 1.

445
00:20:02,030 --> 00:20:04,950
One year old. That's little.

446
00:20:07,750 --> 00:20:09,470
That's my girl.

447
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,760
That's how old you are.

448
00:20:13,090 --> 00:20:14,920
Did I teach her that?

449
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,530
Did I just impart wisdom?

450
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,740
I want one.

451
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,290
Me too.

452
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:30,000
There's no one around.

453
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,340
Why don't we just take this one?

454
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:34,850
- And head to Canada. - I was kidding.

455
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,650
I wasn't. Let's get going.

456
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:40,720
Hey, are Ross and Rachel back?

457
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:41,490
No, not yet.

458
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:43,830
Oh, good, I didn't miss the party.

459
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,460
What about your massage client?

460
00:20:45,510 --> 00:20:47,380
I just felt so bad missing this.

461
00:20:47,430 --> 00:20:49,590
So I just slipped him a little something, you know.

462
00:20:50,610 --> 00:20:52,570
As long as I'm back in five or six hours,

463
00:20:52,570 --> 00:20:53,560
it'll be all right.

464
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:56,870
Okay.

465
00:20:57,450 --> 00:20:59,590
If Ross and Rachel ask,

466
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:01,210
I've been here the whole time. The whole time.

467
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:04,620
I've been here the whole time.

468
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:07,500
Joey, we just saw you come in.

469
00:21:07,550 --> 00:21:09,690
You ran past us on the stairs.

470
00:21:10,830 --> 00:21:12,470
I don't care that you left.

471
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,530
I'm just glad that you're here.

472
00:21:14,530 --> 00:21:15,150
Thanks, you guys.

473
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,080
Hey, guys, come on.

474
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,980
You gotta see what Emma just did.

475
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:20,400
- What? - Emma, how old are you?

476
00:21:20,450 --> 00:21:22,360
How old are you today?

477
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:29,320
Emma, that's right. You're that many.

478
00:21:29,370 --> 00:21:32,210
Oh, my God, our daughter's a genius.

479
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,090
- This means-- - No! No science camp!

480
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:39,470
Damn it! I'll put a candle on the cake.

481
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:43,920
Oh, and, Emma, look at your stuffed animals

482
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,780
lined up so neatly.

483
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:47,460
Thanks.

484
00:21:48,530 --> 00:21:51,190
Okay, here we go.

485
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:55,480
Emma's first birthday cake.

486
00:21:57,090 --> 00:21:58,720
Go ahead, Emma, blow out the candle.

487
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:01,540
Come on, Emma. You can do it.

488
00:22:01,810 --> 00:22:03,540
What's wrong? Are you okay?

489
00:22:03,540 --> 00:22:04,410
Oh, yeah, nothing.

490
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:06,960
These are happy tears.

491
00:22:07,850 --> 00:22:09,730
This is just what I wanted.

492
00:22:11,870 --> 00:22:13,740
Hey, you made it into a bunny.

493
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:17,090
What is wrong with me?

494
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:19,090
It looked more delicious when it was a penis.

495
00:22:26,030 --> 00:22:27,990
- Okay, you ready? - Yeah.

496
00:22:27,990 --> 00:22:30,850
- And record. - Okay.

497
00:22:31,290 --> 00:22:32,640
Hi, Emma.

498
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:35,450
Well, your first birthday is over, and--

499
00:22:35,450 --> 00:22:36,930
Go! Go! Come on!

500
00:22:36,930 --> 00:22:38,750
Go! Go! Come on!

501
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:45,260
Go! Go, Alan! Run, you hairy bastard!

